  "name": "Cem (Alevi-Bektaşi ritual song and semah)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ritual music of the Alevi and Bektaşi cem ceremony of Anatolia, in which a zâkir accompanies himself on the bağlama, treated as sacred in the rite, singing deyiş and nefes hymns by poets such as Pir Sultan Abdal and Hatayi, düvaz-imam hymns naming the Twelve Imams, and the music of the semah, a turning ritual dance performed by men and women together that moves from slow to fast sections. Semah, Alevi-Bektaşi ritual is inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage.",
  "recipe": "classic modern cem, ritual Devotional, Sufi branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. alevi cem devotional saz baglama. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
